WEBVTT

00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:04.520
Good morning.

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:07.150
My name is Minami Chiaki.

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:09.780
I'm the youngest of three sisters.

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:13.320
Though at times I like to
imagine I have only one sister,

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:13.780
unfortunately, there's three of us.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:14.950
<b>Minami Chiaki
Minami Chiaki
unfortunately, there's three of us.</b>

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:16.490
<b>Minami Chiaki
Minami Chiaki</b>

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:25.000
We'll be seeing clear skies
all across the nation...

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.290
C'mon! At least say something funny!

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:27.340
Something like, "Oh, you're already awake?"

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:29.960
<b>Minami Kana
Minami Kana
Something like, "Oh, you're already awake?"</b>

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:31.210
or "you'll catch a cold if you sleep under the kotatsu"!
<b>Minami Kana
Minami Kana</b>

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:32.510
This is the middle sister, Kana.

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:33.010
Minami Kana
Minami Kana

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:35.010
Her name means "summer,"

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:37.350
and she's as sultry and
impetuous as the summer sun.

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:40.100
She's not a sister I'm proud of.

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:43.100
I bet you're thinking something rude about me.

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:45.350
Was not.

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:48.690
I was just thinking about
.how energetic you are today.

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:50.530
Oh? That's okay, then.

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:53.110
All right, time to change.

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:57.780
It's so nice and warm!

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:02.330
How much longer are you
gonna rely on the kotatsu?

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:04.040
It's spring, you know.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:05.580
We have one, so why not use it?

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:08.130
Think of that poor, neglected kotatsu!

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:10.420
Kana! Chiaki!

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:12.050
What's that? The voice of a goddess?

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:14.380
When you're done, let's have breakfast.

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:15.090
I guess not.

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:15.510
Minami Haruka
Minami Haruka

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:17.930
This is the eldest sister, Haruka-neesama.

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:19.180
Her name means "spring,"
<b>Minami Haruka
Minami Haruka</b>

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:21.220
and she's as pleasant and gentle as the spring sun.

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:22.180
I'm very proud of her.
<b>Minami Haruka
Minami Haruka</b>

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:23.770
Sure!

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:25.890
Hey, Kana.

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:28.940
There's no need to change under the kotatsu.

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:31.150
Haruka-neesama, say something too!

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:36.280
Haruka-neesama?

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:39.030
You want me to keep
warming up your coat?

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:40.030
Sure.

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:46.370
We warmed up your uniform too, Chiaki.

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:49.830
Thank you.

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:52.380
It's so warm...

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:56.510
How much longer are you
gonna rely on the kotatsu?

00:01:56.510 --> 00:01:58.680
It's spring, you know.

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:00.430
We have one, so why not use it?

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:02.680
Think of that poor, neglected kotatsu!

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:06.310
All right, let's get changed and have breakfast.

00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:11.810
Let's eat!

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:45.620
All right!

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:48.490
Let's head to school with a spring in our step!

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:49.830
By the way, Kana.

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:51.910
Aren't you getting your test results back today?

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:56.540
Ow, ow, ow! My stomach!

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:58.840
It hurts so bad I'm gonna have to take today off!

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:01.170
Please, go on without me.

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:03.380
Don't forget to show me the results, okay?

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:06.890
Okay.

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:11.890
Skipping school today won't
change the mark you got, moron.

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:13.900
Spring Is Here, And So Are The Minamis
Spring Is Here, And So Are The Minamis

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:15.940
We're off!

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:17.400
Spring Is Here, And So Are The Minamis
Spring Is Here, And So Are The Minamis

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:21.650
Minami Kana

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:25.780
Once again, I've received a score that boldly depicts the frailty of the human condition.

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:28.530
I don't think I can show this to Haruka.

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:31.750
If I don't get it together by
the next test, it'll be bad.

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:32.870
It'll be very bad.

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:35.630
That's it! I'll ask someone to teach me!

00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:36.750
Monthly Test

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:38.040
Keiko.

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:40.880
Help me study.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:42.260
No way.

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:44.090
You never take it seriously.

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:46.510
It's different today.

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:49.260
Look at me. Are these the eyes of
someone who isn't <i>deadly</i> serious?

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:53.140
Sorry. I don't have my
.glasses on at the moment.

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:55.480
Huh? That's strange.

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:57.100
Could've sworn you had
.them on a second ago.

00:04:57.610 --> 00:05:00.820
She turned down my request for help.

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:02.610
That's right!

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:07.870
Haruka, let's go to the beach.

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:11.160
Do you want to go, Chiaki?

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:13.000
Yes, I do.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.710
All right! Let's go, then.

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:21.210
Seems like sincerity is more important
.than seriousness when asking for help.

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:24.970
Miyuki-chan, Miyuki-chan!

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:28.090
Huh? What's up?

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:32.060
You're about as tall as Chiaki.

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:33.720
What is it?

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:36.890
You have really honest eyes.

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:37.980
Do I?

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:39.520
Miyuki-chan.

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:41.230
Sorry to ask this out of nowhere,

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:43.940
but you didn't do so well
on your test, did you?

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:45.610
You're not sorry at all!

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:49.530
I know how you can
.improve your grades.

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:50.620
Really?

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:54.290
Keiko, can you help Miyuki study?

00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:56.790
You can use my house.

00:05:57.830 --> 00:06:00.460
Keiko-chan, please!

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:05.460
Well, I guess I can't say no to you.

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:06.470
Perfect.

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:08.470
Like that?

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:10.260
Yep, yep! That was perfect!

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:12.560
I expected nothing less from you.

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:18.190
I just don't get it.

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:20.190
Keiko, can you help me with this part?

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:22.690
Just read it over again and think carefully.

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:25.440
Keiko-chan, can you help me with this part?

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:26.740
Please?

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:30.410
Oh, well. You just do this here,

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:31.700
then this, and...

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:32.740
No fair!

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:35.410
Why are you helping her but not me?!

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:38.370
Because I'm here to help <i>her</i> study.

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:41.130
Kana-chan, don't get so mad.

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:42.500
Please?

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:43.920
Why, you little...

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:46.670
Only kids get to have other people solve all their problems for them!

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:51.180
The whole reason you study is so that you can overcome challenges on your own!

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:56.220
You're absolutely right, Kana-chan!

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:58.520
I'll work hard and study by myself!

00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:00.440
All right! You do that!

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:02.020
I'm going home too.

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:03.690
Sure. See you tomorrow.

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:09.820
Oh, crap!

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:12.990
Name:
Monthly Test
Minami Kana

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:14.620
That's one point less than last time.

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:18.370
It really is impossible to improve on your own.

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:21.580
I guess humans have to work
.together to achieve something.

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:22.830
Kana-chan!

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:26.880
Thanks to you, I got my first hundred!

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:28.760
So you can do anything
you put your mind to?!

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:30.800
By the way, Kana-chan.

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:32.720
Could you tell me how to grow taller?

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:35.640
Fine, but only if you help me study in exchange.

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:37.560
We humans have to work together.

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:40.310
Keiko, help me study?

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:41.560
No way.

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:55.950
Yeah.
He
said
he
liked it.
Thanks,
man.

00:07:57.740 --> 00:07:59.250
Love
Now

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:03.370
Kana-chan, are you sure you don't have to study?

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:06.250
Didn't you say you felt bitter about your grades?

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:08.750
It was a score that depicted the frailty of the human condition.

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:10.130
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:13.430
Aren't you here for Chiaki's help anyway?

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:15.340
It's fine.

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:18.760
I'm going to the bathroom, Chiaki.

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:26.060
That Uchida.

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:29.070
She really left her donut here, unguarded.

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:32.990
This is the perfect time to teach
.her how cruel the world can be.

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:37.910
Chiaki never notices anything that happens around her when she's busy studying.

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:39.910
All right.

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:54.050
My donut is gone!

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:57.140
And I'd been saving it for last...

00:08:57.140 --> 00:08:59.140
I was looking forward to it too.

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:02.180
It was you! I know you can't resist
donuts from that store, Kana-chan!

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:04.690
I didn't take it.

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:06.810
I can hear you chewing it!

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:09.360
It wasn't me.

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:13.070
You just swallowed it!

00:09:13.610 --> 00:09:15.110
You saw that, right, Chiaki?!

00:09:15.110 --> 00:09:16.450
It was Kana-chan, right?!

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:21.160
Sorry, but when Chiaki's busy studying, nothing can disrupt her focus.

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:22.450
That's ridiculous!

00:09:22.450 --> 00:09:26.460
I wonder how dinner's coming along.

00:09:40.220 --> 00:09:40.970
Huh?

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:44.230
I was reading volume 10
.of my manga, but it's gone.

00:09:44.230 --> 00:09:48.100
Are you sure you even had
that volume to begin with?

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:51.650
Hang on, isn't that volume 10 you're reading right there?

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:54.320
Hey, Chiaki, that's my manga, right?

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:58.990
Kana-chan, when Chiaki's busy studying,
nothing can disrupt her focus.

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:01.700
That's what I just said to you!

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:04.250
Chiaki, could you come here for a moment?

00:10:04.250 --> 00:10:05.750
Coming!

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:13.380
Could you taste this?

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:15.340
Yes, Haruka-neesama.

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:17.680
It tasted perfect.

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:27.600
Huh?

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:31.270
Kana and Uchida seem to have
.fallen into a depressed silence.

00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:33.320
Could this be...

00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:35.480
They definitely did something.

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:36.940
Something bad.

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:37.860
What?

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:40.870
You completely ignored
.them earlier, after all.

00:10:40.870 --> 00:10:42.870
They must've done something.

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:44.740
You weren't ignoring them.

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:46.200
You just didn't feel like responding.

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:48.410
That's ignoring them.

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:49.620
Let's see...

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:52.330
They'd probably try to pull something like...

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:53.960
hiding your pencil?

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:55.800
It's there.

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:58.970
And... so is your eraser.

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:03.760
Look at that!

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:07.060
Uchida's trying not to laugh!

00:11:07.060 --> 00:11:09.890
She wants to see how long
it takes before you realize!

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:12.730
So it's Uchida, that mean-spirited girl.

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:14.900
We need to figure out what she did.

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:16.530
Yes!

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:17.690
She's so mean!

00:11:18.110 --> 00:11:20.740
Did she doodle on one of the pages?

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:24.070
Or fill all the problems out incorrectly?

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:40.590
I can't take it anymore.

00:11:40.590 --> 00:11:44.180
I'm sorry I tried to study on my own.

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:45.640
It's just too awkward!

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:47.850
Oh, thank goodness.

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:50.940
It was starting to get to me too.

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:54.440
I know you told me to be quiet when Chiaki was studying,

00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:57.730
but you kept making that weird face and it was all I could do not to laugh!

00:11:57.730 --> 00:11:59.610
I wasn't trying to make a
weird face! That's mean!

00:11:59.610 --> 00:12:02.740
Do you know how much
effort it took to keep quiet?

00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:03.860
I knew it!

00:12:03.860 --> 00:12:06.950
I knew you were being quiet because of me!

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:09.040
Okay...

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:12.290
Dinner's ready.

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:15.710
I've got a good feeling about this one, especially since Chiaki tasted it.

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:18.090
If you'd like some, please join us.

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:19.420
Thank you.

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:21.800
Haruka-neesama's cooking is spectacular.

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:23.050
Really?

00:12:23.050 --> 00:12:23.090
You'll want to have thirds!
Really?

00:12:23.090 --> 00:12:24.840
You'll want to have thirds!

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:27.100
I can't eat that much.

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:29.600
She's being extra nice now.

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:32.020
She doesn't know how to
.make it up to her friend.

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:35.230
Haruka-neesama, give Uchida
an extra-large helping!

00:12:35.230 --> 00:12:37.020
I said I can't eat that much!

00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:50.040
I went to the shrine the other day,

00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:53.540
and since I had some extra money I decided to get a fortune.

00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:57.080
It says something about "the person I await."

00:12:57.790 --> 00:13:00.250
"The person I await" usually
means a lover, right?

00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:01.630
Right?

00:13:01.630 --> 00:13:02.260
Right?!

00:13:02.590 --> 00:13:03.760
I think so.

00:13:04.470 --> 00:13:08.640
So what does "shall alight
without prior dispatch" mean?

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:09.890
Is he coming?

00:13:09.890 --> 00:13:11.060
Is he not?

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:16.060
I think "prior dispatch" means sending a
.letter or making a phone call in advance.

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:17.060
Correspondence

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:19.060
In this case, dispatch means "correspondence."
Correspondence

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:23.070
So it means my lover will appear before me without any warning?!

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:25.490
You can think of it like that.

00:13:25.490 --> 00:13:29.070
Oh, it also says you should concentrate on
.your own study instead of relying on others.

00:13:29.070 --> 00:13:32.120
I see. So he'll finally appear...

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:35.250
So you really <i>did</i> want a boyfriend.

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:39.380
Fujioka-kun, this is your chance.

00:13:39.380 --> 00:13:41.250
Go for it already.

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:52.890
If he could show up at any moment, I'll need to make sure I'm ready.

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:56.390
But what should I do to prepare?

00:13:56.390 --> 00:13:57.690
Hey, Kana-chan!

00:13:59.060 --> 00:14:01.770
Oh, Miyuki. You scared me.

00:14:01.770 --> 00:14:04.570
You just appeared without prior dispatch.

00:14:04.570 --> 00:14:05.820
Hey, Kana-chan,

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:08.030
could you tell me how to grow taller?

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:09.660
I'm a bit busy right now.

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:10.910
Go ask Riko.

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:11.530
Huh?

00:14:11.530 --> 00:14:13.040
'kay!

00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:15.910
Hey, Riko-chan,

00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:18.500
could you tell me how to
make my boobs bigger?

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:21.420
Huh? Why are you asking me?

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:23.670
Because everyone says
.that yours are amazing.

00:14:23.670 --> 00:14:26.170
I don't think that's true, but...

00:14:26.170 --> 00:14:29.010
They say you put a lot of effort into it.

00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:30.390
Really?

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:31.550
I see.

00:14:31.550 --> 00:14:35.430
So being prepared means working to improve the parts of yourself that are lacking.

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:38.230
But what am I lacking in?

00:14:38.230 --> 00:14:39.310
Brains?

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:40.350
No, no, no.

00:14:40.350 --> 00:14:42.440
I'm really a genius who just plays dumb.

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:46.440
Chiaki said I was a genius in a good way.

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:47.650
Minami!

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:51.160
Wha... What do you want?!

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:52.160
Is something wrong?

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:54.410
It can't be... Is it...

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:57.910
The person I await who shall
...alight without prior dispatch...

00:14:57.910 --> 00:15:00.710
It's Fujioka?

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:04.380
What are you doing in my seat?

00:15:05.460 --> 00:15:07.880
I'm tired of thinking. I'm taking a break.

00:15:08.380 --> 00:15:09.880
I see...

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:11.930
Chiaki-chan.

00:15:12.340 --> 00:15:13.600
What's wrong?

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:16.060
I've asked you here for one reason and one reason alone.

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:18.560
There are mandarins on top of the kotatsu.

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:19.810
So there are.

00:15:19.810 --> 00:15:25.400
But I have to hold onto Fujioka here. He was given to me by Santa.

00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:27.570
Oh right, that teddy bear's name is Fujioka too.

00:15:27.570 --> 00:15:31.320
If I were to peel those mandarins,
.the skin would turn my fingers yellow.

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:33.870
What do you think will happen if I touch Fujioka afterward?

00:15:33.870 --> 00:15:36.330
You'll turn Fujioka the Bear
yellow as well, won't you?

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:38.830
I don't want to see him turn yellow.

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:40.080
What should I do?

00:15:41.830 --> 00:15:43.330
Why don't I peel them for you?

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:46.040
Then feed me the mandarins.

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:48.550
Sure, sure.

00:15:49.590 --> 00:15:51.340
Chiaki.

00:15:51.840 --> 00:15:53.140
Fujioka!

00:15:53.140 --> 00:15:54.390
When did you get here?

00:15:54.800 --> 00:15:56.510
Oh, hey, Minami.

00:15:57.680 --> 00:16:00.480
Could it really be Fujioka?

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:03.150
Have a safe trip home.

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:04.940
Sure. Thank you.

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:08.530
Could Fujioka really be the one?

00:16:20.790 --> 00:16:22.330
Hello.

00:16:22.330 --> 00:16:24.540
Oh, the key for your bicycle lock?

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:26.420
You left it here.

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:30.420
If you want, I can bring it downstairs for you.

00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:33.010
Oh, you'll come up for it?

00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:34.130
Okay.

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:35.890
Yeah, this is it!

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:36.680
Thank you!

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:40.520
He called before he came.
That counts as a dispatch.

00:16:41.680 --> 00:16:43.270
So it's not Fujioka.

00:16:43.690 --> 00:16:45.310
What's that about?

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:46.480
Dinner's ready!

00:16:47.190 --> 00:16:48.730
A dispatch has alighted!

00:16:49.190 --> 00:16:51.820
Fujioka-kun, could you tell me how to get bigger?

00:16:51.820 --> 00:16:53.740
Wait, what?!

00:16:53.740 --> 00:16:56.370
You always appear without prior dispatch, Miyuki.

00:16:56.370 --> 00:16:59.160
Wait, is it Miyuki?!

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:02.700
All right!

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:05.120
Today's nice and warm,
so let's put away the kotatsu!

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:08.540
Kana, let's just keep it out.

00:17:08.540 --> 00:17:11.090
It might get cold again.

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:11.960
No way.

00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:13.090
We put it away today!

00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:17.510
This is a perfect day to put away the kotatsu. We must take full advantage of it.

00:17:17.510 --> 00:17:20.760
Besides, we fight about when
.to put it away every year.

00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:24.020
K-Kana's actually being responsible...

00:17:24.020 --> 00:17:26.020
No! I want to keep it out!

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:29.520
And Haruka-neesama's the one who's whining!

00:17:30.770 --> 00:17:32.730
C'mon, let's put it away today!

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:35.610
The weather's nice, and we can air the kotatsu cover out.

00:17:35.610 --> 00:17:36.990
No means no!

00:17:36.990 --> 00:17:39.120
I don't care what you say!

00:17:39.620 --> 00:17:43.200
I like how the kotatsu sits there, unmoving!

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:45.330
I-Is that so?

00:17:45.870 --> 00:17:47.040
Chiaki,

00:17:47.040 --> 00:17:49.040
we're going to get Haruka out of there.

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:50.130
Give me a hand.

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:52.340
We don't need to yet.

00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:54.840
Why do you want to put it away so badly?

00:17:55.630 --> 00:17:58.590
Because the kotatsu... is dangerous.

00:17:59.050 --> 00:18:00.970
It makes people lazy!

00:18:00.970 --> 00:18:03.600
It sucks them in and never lets them go!

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:07.350
If we don't get Haruka out,
.she'll never make us dinner.

00:18:07.350 --> 00:18:12.730
Haruka-neesama already works so hard
doing everything around the house for us.

00:18:13.110 --> 00:18:16.240
Can't we just let her relax for a bit?

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:19.530
I see you still don't understand Haruka at all.

00:18:19.530 --> 00:18:21.200
What do you mean?

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:25.700
If it weren't for us, how much lazier do you think Haruka would be?

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:29.920
The only thing which can expose Haruka's true nature to the world is... the kotatsu!

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:38.430
Do you really mean to parade before the world this side of Haruka that must never be seen?

00:18:38.430 --> 00:18:39.930
That's...

00:18:40.890 --> 00:18:41.890
Chiaki.

00:18:41.890 --> 00:18:45.640
We're getting her out of
.that kotatsu for <i>her</i> sake.

00:18:45.640 --> 00:18:48.020
For Haruka-neesama's sake...

00:18:48.940 --> 00:18:50.480
Fine.

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:52.020
I'll help you.

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:53.150
All right!

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:55.030
Time to get her out of there!

00:18:55.780 --> 00:18:59.400
First, we cut the power to the kotatsu!

00:18:59.400 --> 00:19:02.320
You needed my help for that?

00:19:02.320 --> 00:19:04.950
Then we lift the sheets!

00:19:04.950 --> 00:19:07.750
You needed my help for that?

00:19:08.580 --> 00:19:10.000
And now we wait.

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:13.250
You needed my help for that?

00:19:16.250 --> 00:19:18.720
No reaction at all.

00:19:18.720 --> 00:19:19.880
She's not budging.

00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:22.010
We've already disabled
.the kotatsu's functions.

00:19:23.140 --> 00:19:25.390
This is our last resort.

00:19:25.390 --> 00:19:27.470
We separate them by
moving the kotatsu!

00:19:27.470 --> 00:19:28.350
Got it.

00:19:28.350 --> 00:19:30.640
I'll stand here and watch.

00:19:40.360 --> 00:19:41.910
No resistance.

00:19:44.030 --> 00:19:44.910
I won!

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:47.910
She lost to my aggression!

00:19:47.910 --> 00:19:49.040
Woohoo!

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:49.200
I did it! Woohoo! I did it!

00:19:49.200 --> 00:19:55.630
No, you're the one who doesn't
understand Haruka-neesama at all, Kana.

00:19:55.630 --> 00:19:57.710
This is the culmination of laziness.

00:19:57.710 --> 00:20:00.510
She was too lazy to even follow the kotatsu.

00:20:00.510 --> 00:20:04.220
I'm sure she had no intention of fighting you from the start.

00:20:04.220 --> 00:20:05.350
Hooray! Hooray! Hooray! Hooray!

00:20:05.350 --> 00:20:08.770
Haruka-neesama, please be
.as lazy as you want to be.
Hooray! Hooray! Hooray! Hooray!

00:20:08.770 --> 00:20:09.470
Haruka-neesama, please be
.as lazy as you want to be.

00:20:12.310 --> 00:20:13.980
You put your kotatsu away already?

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:16.480
Yeah. It was pretty warm yesterday.

00:20:16.480 --> 00:20:19.650
You guys argue about it every year,
so I'm surprised it happened so quickly.

00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:21.490
Well, I wouldn't say we argue.

00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:23.820
But isn't today a bit cold?

00:20:23.820 --> 00:20:26.490
Don't you want to take it out again?

00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:30.870
You really don't think about getting into it again once you put it away. I think we'll be fine.

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:35.460
A stag beetle?

00:20:35.460 --> 00:20:37.380
Oh, welcome home.

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:40.880
Kana, didn't we put the
kotatsu away yesterday?

00:20:40.880 --> 00:20:43.470
Huh? But it's cold today.

00:20:43.970 --> 00:20:45.140
By the way, Haruka,

00:20:45.510 --> 00:20:47.640
why not bring your clothes under the kotatsu

00:20:48.010 --> 00:20:51.640
and get changed with me in warm, cozy comfort over the next hour?

00:20:53.310 --> 00:20:55.560
Oh, I forgot my own change of clothes.

00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:58.320
Sorry, Haruka, could you grab me some—

00:20:59.230 --> 00:21:00.110
Here we go.

00:21:00.110 --> 00:21:00.610
It's cold! It's col—
Here we go.

00:21:00.610 --> 00:21:00.980
I caught myself a big stag beetle!
It's cold! It's col—

00:21:00.980 --> 00:21:03.700
It's cold!
I caught myself a big stag beetle!

00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:06.030
Oh, a hot pot!

00:21:06.030 --> 00:21:09.200
It's cold outside, so eat up, okay?

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:09.910
Okay.

00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:15.540
I'd appreciate it if you gave me
.more meat than vegetables.

00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:17.880
You still hate vegetables?

00:21:17.880 --> 00:21:19.380
You're not in elementary
.school anymore, you know—

00:21:19.380 --> 00:21:20.800
Yes I am!

00:21:20.800 --> 00:21:22.260
All right!

00:21:22.260 --> 00:21:27.890
Allow this wonderful sister of whom you are so very proud to feed you some vegetables.

00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:29.390
Here. Open wide.

00:21:29.390 --> 00:21:30.510
I'm not eating those raw!

00:21:30.510 --> 00:21:32.140
The least you could do is cook them!

00:21:32.140 --> 00:21:34.560
Hey, stop that.

00:21:34.560 --> 00:21:36.020
Okay.

00:21:36.390 --> 00:21:38.020
Well, let's eat.

00:21:38.480 --> 00:21:40.520
Thanks for the food!

00:21:41.480 --> 00:21:48.070
This story is a simple illustration of the three
.Minami sisters and the ordinary life they lead.

00:21:48.070 --> 00:21:51.030
Please don't expect too much from it.

00:23:21.670 --> 00:23:23.000
It's spring, but it's still cold outside.

00:23:23.000 --> 00:23:26.630
What should a skirt-wearing high school girl do at a time like this?

00:23:26.630 --> 00:23:27.510
Wear a tracksuit?

00:23:27.510 --> 00:23:29.130
My pride will not allow it!

00:23:29.130 --> 00:23:31.180
The correct answer was, "Just deal with it!"

00:23:31.180 --> 00:23:32.800
Next time: "Let's Be Ourselves."

00:23:32.800 --> 00:23:36.010
Couldn't I just wear bloomers?
